From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:12:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] servoshell: Drop an unmet lint expectation of the embedded
 app

`App::update_user_interface_state` expected `unused_variables` unless
both the `tracing` and `tracing-hitrace` features are enabled, since
`state` was only read for a hitrace marker. Since c73bea970da (#48393)
it is also read for `memory_output` in every configuration, so the
expectation is never fulfilled, and an OpenHarmony or Android build
with `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings"` fails with
`unfulfilled_lint_expectations`. CI builds those platforms without
`-D warnings`, so it went unnoticed. Remove the expectation.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: no test; it removes a lint attribute.

Validation: `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --locked --ohos
--profile checked-release` fails with the unfulfilled expectation
without this patch and builds with it.

AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; found with the local CI checks)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs b/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
index 61b036e934f..116c53dd49d 100644
--- a/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
+++ b/ports/servoshell/egl/app.rs
@@ -80,10 +80,6 @@ impl PlatformWindow for EmbeddedPlatformWindow {
         false
     }
 
-    #[cfg_attr(
-        not(all(feature = "tracing", feature = "tracing-hitrace")),
-        expect(unused_variables)
-    )]
     fn update_user_interface_state(
         &self,
         state: &RunningAppState,
